IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa18-part23-ch1`

-- coa18-part23-ch2.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 23 (distributions), Chapter 2 (justification of
-- distribution by reference to accounts), ss 836 to 840. Lines 11235-11303 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. Layer 1: the law,
-- objectively. How to read an answer (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, NOTHING) is as in the header of coa18-part22-notice.l4.
-- It imports coa18-part23-ch1 for the type `s 831(3) kind of relevant accounts` (Companies Act accounts, IAS accounts).
--
-- SEAMS (inputs): `s 423 ...` (circulation of accounts to members), `s 414 ...` (signature of the balance sheet),
-- `ss 395 to 397 ...` (properly prepared), `s 396 ...` (provisions specified by regulations), `Part 35 ...` (certified
-- translation), `s 4(2) the company is a public company`, `s 677`, `s 678`, `s 679`, `s 705` (Part 18).
-- ANSWER OTHER PARTS ASK FOR (PLAN section 6): `s 836(2) the relevant accounts for the distribution` (the type below).

§ `Part 23 (ss 829 to 853), Chapter 2: ss 836 to 840`

§§ `s 836 Justification of distribution by reference to relevant accounts`

DECLARE `s 836(1) item stated in the relevant accounts` IS ONE OF
    `s 836(1)(a) profits, losses, assets and liabilities`
    `s 836(1)(b) provisions`
    `s 836(1)(c) share capital and reserves (including undistributable reserves)`
    `s 836(1) another item`

-- src:11238 | (1) Whether a distribution may be made by a company without contravening this Part is determined by reference to the following items as stated in the relevant accounts—
-- src:11239 | (a) profits, losses, assets and liabilities;
-- src:11240 | (b) provisions of the following kinds—
-- src:11241 | (i) where the relevant accounts are Companies Act accounts, provisions of a kind specified for the purposes of this subsection by regulations under section 396;
-- src:11242 | (ii) where the relevant accounts are IAS accounts, provisions of any kind;
-- src:11243 | (c) share capital and reserves (including undistributable reserves).
@ref s 836(1) Justification of distribution by reference to relevant accounts (src:11238-11243)
GIVEN item IS A `s 836(1) item stated in the relevant accounts`
      accounts IS A `s 831(3) kind of relevant accounts`
      `s 396 the provision is of a kind specified for the purposes of section 836(1) by regulations under section 396` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 836(1) whether a distribution may be made is determined by reference to the item as stated in the relevant accounts` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `s 836(1)(a) profits, losses, assets and liabilities` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 836(1)(b) provisions` THEN
        CONSIDER accounts
        WHEN `s 831(3)(a) Companies Act accounts` THEN
            CONSIDER `s 396 the provision is of a kind specified for the purposes of section 836(1) by regulations under section 396`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "(i) where the relevant accounts are Companies Act accounts, provisions of a kind specified for the purposes of this subsection by regulations under section 396": the kinds are in s 396 (outside this Part)
        WHEN `s 831(3)(b) IAS accounts` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names Companies Act accounts and IAS accounts only
    WHEN `s 836(1)(c) share capital and reserves (including undistributable reserves)` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "by reference to the following items" lists three; the subsection does not say "only"

DECLARE `s 836(2) accounts` IS ONE OF
    `s 836(2) the company's last annual accounts`
    `s 836(2)(a) interim accounts`
    `s 836(2)(b) initial accounts`

-- src:11244 | (2) The relevant accounts are the company's last annual accounts, except that—
-- src:11245 | (a) where the distribution would be found to contravene this Part by reference to the company's last annual accounts, it may be justified by reference to interim accounts, and
-- src:11246 | (b) where the distribution is proposed to be declared during the company's first accounting reference period, or before any accounts have been circulated in respect of that period, it may be justified by reference to initial accounts.
@ref s 836(2) Justification of distribution by reference to relevant accounts (src:11244-11246)
GIVEN `the distribution would be found to contravene this Part by reference to the company's last annual accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 836(2)(a) the distribution may be justified by reference to interim accounts` MEANS
    IF `the distribution would be found to contravene this Part by reference to the company's last annual accounts`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the distribution would be found to contravene this Part by reference to the company's last annual accounts, it may be justified by reference to interim accounts" ("where" fails)

@ref s 836(2)(b) Justification of distribution by reference to relevant accounts (src:11246-11246)
GIVEN `the distribution is proposed to be declared during the company's first accounting reference period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the distribution is proposed to be declared before any accounts have been circulated in respect of that period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 836(2)(b) the distribution may be justified by reference to initial accounts` MEANS
    IF `the distribution is proposed to be declared during the company's first accounting reference period` OR `the distribution is proposed to be declared before any accounts have been circulated in respect of that period`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the distribution is proposed to be declared during the company's first accounting reference period, or before any accounts have been circulated in respect of that period, it may be justified by reference to initial accounts" ("where" fails)

@ref s 836(2) Justification of distribution by reference to relevant accounts (src:11244-11246)
GIVEN `the distribution would be found to contravene this Part by reference to the company's last annual accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the distribution is proposed to be declared during the company's first accounting reference period or before any accounts have been circulated in respect of that period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 836(2) the relevant accounts are the company's last annual accounts` MEANS
    IF     (NOT `the distribution would be found to contravene this Part by reference to the company's last annual accounts`)
       AND (NOT `the distribution is proposed to be declared during the company's first accounting reference period or before any accounts have been circulated in respect of that period`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The relevant accounts are the company's last annual accounts, except that ... it may be justified by reference to interim accounts ... initial accounts": a permission to use other accounts, so the text does not say which accounts are used

DECLARE `s 836(3) section whose requirements must be complied with` IS ONE OF
    `s 836(3) section 837 (last annual accounts)`
    `s 836(3) section 838 (interim accounts)`
    `s 836(3) section 839 (initial accounts)`

-- src:11247 | (3) The requirements of—
-- src:11248 | section 837 (as regards the company's last annual accounts),
-- src:11249 | section 838 (as regards interim accounts), and
-- src:11250 | section 839 (as regards initial accounts),
-- src:11251 | must be complied with, as and where applicable.
@ref s 836(3) Justification of distribution by reference to relevant accounts (src:11247-11251)
GIVEN accounts IS A `s 836(2) accounts`
GIVETH A `s 836(3) section whose requirements must be complied with`
`s 836(3) the section whose requirements must be complied with as regards the accounts` MEANS
    CONSIDER accounts
    WHEN `s 836(2) the company's last annual accounts` THEN `s 836(3) section 837 (last annual accounts)`
    WHEN `s 836(2)(a) interim accounts` THEN `s 836(3) section 838 (interim accounts)`
    WHEN `s 836(2)(b) initial accounts` THEN `s 836(3) section 839 (initial accounts)`

-- src:11252 | (4) If any applicable requirement of those sections is not complied with, the accounts may not be relied on for the purposes of this Part and the distribution is accordingly treated as contravening this Part.
@ref s 836(4) Justification of distribution by reference to relevant accounts (src:11252-11252)
GIVEN `an applicable requirement of those sections is not complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 836(4) the accounts may not be relied on for the purposes of this Part and the distribution is treated as contravening this Part` MEANS
    IF `an applicable requirement of those sections is not complied with`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If any applicable requirement of those sections is not complied with, the accounts may not be relied on for the purposes of this Part and the distribution is accordingly treated as contravening this Part."

§§ `s 837 Requirements where last annual accounts used`

-- src:11255 | (1) The company's last annual accounts means the company's individual accounts—
-- src:11256 | (a) that were last circulated to members in accordance with section 423 (duty to circulate copies of annual accounts and reports), or
-- src:11257 | (b) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
@ref s 837(1) Requirements where last annual accounts used (src:11255-11257)
GIVEN `the accounts are the company's individual accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 423 the accounts were last circulated to members in accordance with section 423` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 837(1) the accounts are the company's last annual accounts` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the accounts are the company's individual accounts`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company's last annual accounts means the company's individual accounts"
        OTHERWISE `s 423 the accounts were last circulated to members in accordance with section 423` -- JUST FALSE here is the text's "means ... that were last circulated to members in accordance with section 423"; NOTHING stays NOTHING (points outside the text, s 423); (b) is shown as dots in the text

-- src:11258 | (2) The accounts must have been properly prepared in accordance with this Act, or have been so prepared subject only to matters that are not material for determining (by reference to the items mentioned in section 836(1)) whether the distribution would contravene this Part.
@ref s 837(2) Requirements where last annual accounts used (src:11258-11258)
GIVEN `the accounts have been properly prepared in accordance with this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accounts have been so prepared subject only to matters that are not material for determining whether the distribution would contravene this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 837(2) the accounts were prepared as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the accounts have been properly prepared in accordance with this Act` OR `the accounts have been so prepared subject only to matters that are not material for determining whether the distribution would contravene this Part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The accounts must have been properly prepared in accordance with this Act, or have been so prepared subject only to matters that are not material for determining (by reference to the items mentioned in section 836(1)) whether the distribution would contravene this Part."

-- src:11259 | (3) Unless the company is exempt from audit and the directors take advantage of that exemption, the auditor must have made his report on the accounts.
@ref s 837(3) Requirements where last annual accounts used (src:11259-11259)
GIVEN `the company is exempt from audit and the directors take advantage of that exemption` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor has made his report on the accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 837(3) the audit requirement is met` MEANS
    IF `the company is exempt from audit and the directors take advantage of that exemption` OR `the auditor has made his report on the accounts`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless the company is exempt from audit and the directors take advantage of that exemption, the auditor must have made his report on the accounts."

-- src:11260 | (4) If that report was qualified—
-- src:11261 | (a) the auditor must have stated in writing (either at the time of his report or subsequently) whether in his opinion the matters in respect of which his report is qualified are material for determining whether a distribution would contravene this Part, and
-- src:11262 | (b) a copy of that statement must—
-- src:11263 | (i) in the case of a private company, have been circulated to members in accordance with section 423, or
-- src:11264 | (ii) in the case of a public company, have been laid before the company in general meeting.
@ref s 837(4) Requirements where last annual accounts used (src:11260-11264)
GIVEN `the report was qualified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor has stated in writing (either at the time of his report or subsequently) whether in his opinion the matters in respect of which his report is qualified are material for determining whether a distribution would contravene this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 423 a copy of that statement was circulated to members in accordance with section 423` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a copy of that statement was laid before the company in general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 837(4) the requirements as to a qualified report are met` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the report was qualified`) THEN JUST TRUE -- no requirement arises: the subsection begins "If that report was qualified"
        IF (NOT `the auditor has stated in writing (either at the time of his report or subsequently) whether in his opinion the matters in respect of which his report is qualified are material for determining whether a distribution would contravene this Part`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) the auditor must have stated in writing (either at the time of his report or subsequently) whether in his opinion the matters in respect of which his report is qualified are material"
        IF `s 4(2) the company is a public company` THEN (IF `a copy of that statement was laid before the company in general meeting` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) a copy of that statement must— ... (ii) in the case of a public company, have been laid before the company in general meeting"
        OTHERWISE `s 423 a copy of that statement was circulated to members in accordance with section 423` -- JUST FALSE here is the text's "(i) in the case of a private company, have been circulated to members in accordance with section 423"; NOTHING stays NOTHING (points outside the text, s 423)

-- src:11265 | (5) An auditor's statement is sufficient for the purposes of a distribution if it relates to distributions of a description that includes the distribution in question, even if at the time of the statement it had not been proposed.
@ref s 837(5) Requirements where last annual accounts used (src:11265-11265)
GIVEN `the statement relates to distributions of a description that includes the distribution in question` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 837(5) the auditor's statement is sufficient for the purposes of a distribution` MEANS
    IF `the statement relates to distributions of a description that includes the distribution in question`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An auditor's statement is sufficient for the purposes of a distribution if it relates to distributions of a description that includes the distribution in question, even if at the time of the statement it had not been proposed": a statement of another kind is not mentioned

